    "requirement_contract": "Eine Baseline MUSS für jedes enthaltene Artefakt ID, Revision, kanonischen SHA-256-Hash und den Pfad seines Snapshotobjekts im Baseline-Objektspeicher speichern.",
    "scope": "10.a.W introduces immutable SnapshotObject and ObjectReference values with exact SHA-256, byte length and archive/objects/<hh>/<sha256> paths. JSON uses the existing strict reader and RFC-8785 canonical bytes; attachment bytes remain untouched. The physical preparation store is restricted to an existing private owned root outside every declared protected boundary and project ancestor. It uses the existing native root-inode mutex, guarded directory traversal, exclusive durable temporary writes and atomic no-replace publication. Identical bytes reuse the existing object; malformed or corrupted targets are rejected without replacement. Reads verify exact length/hash without writes and can inspect an existing project archive. Independent tests cover canonical/opaque bytes, real deduplication, distinct objects, protected-root boundaries, absence of project writes, complete publication, retained failed preparation, busy locks, reopening in a new isolated process and portable distribution behavior. This is the object layer and external preparation store, not a Baseline manifest or normative create command. Complete Baseline identity/revision/scope/configuration bindings, referenced-deletion policy and journalled project publication remain in subsequent steps; no full requirement, full-suite or release success is claimed. Protected-boundary checks are independent of unrelated Git ancestry; a Git marker alone never defines a SpecRoad project root."
  },
